%N A053870 Number of acyclic orientations of the Hamming graph (K_n) x (K_n).
%C A053870 This number is equivalent to the number of plans (i.e. structural solutions) of the open shop problem with n jobs and n machines - see problems in scheduling theory.
%C A053870 In other words, a(n) is the number of acyclic orientations in the n X n rook graph. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 24 2026
%D A053870 Martin Harborth, Structural analysis of shop scheduling problems, PhD thesis, Otto-von-Guericke-Univ. Magdeburg, GCA-Verlag, 1999. (in German)
%H A053870 H. Bräsel, M. Harborth, T. Tautenhahn and P. Willenius, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1018938915709">On the set of solutions of the open shop problem</a>, Ann. Oper. Res. 92 (1999) 241-263.
%H A053870 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RookGraph.html">Rook Graph</a>.
%Y A053870 Cf. A054583, A054652, A054653.
%K A053870 nonn,nice,hard,more,changed
%O A053870 1,2
%A A053870 Martin Harborth (Martin.Harborth(AT)vt.siemens.de)
